        <p class="distnote" id="distnote" hidden></p>
        <p class="legend">
          <b>Method:</b> shortages are matched against the supplier backlog (“BL Fournisseur” inbound), first ordered first served, after French stock (Logtex Moussey, WLOGM) has been allocated by priority — Pacific, Umnyama, Niala, Getro, Sports Life, then first ordered first served — once the domestic market reserve for the next 3 months is set aside. On top of the supplier file, <b>purchase-order updates confirmed by the purchasing team</b> override the dates: a PO confirmed ex-factory switches its lines to available, and a PO with no firm ex-factory date shows the window announced by the supplier instead of a single date.
          <b>Confirmed</b> = a supplier arrival covers the line · <b>Partial</b> = partly covered · <b>Supplier delay</b> = arrival expected on a date already passed · <b>To be confirmed</b> = no supplier order behind it.
          The site shown on each block is the pick-up / shipping site, with its warehouse code: France <code>WLOGM</code>, China <code>WSFCN</code>, Thailand <code>WDTTH</code>, Cambodia <code>WTAKH</code>, Madagascar <code>WCOMG</code>. Cambodia (<code>WTAKH</code>) is kept out of every calculation: it appears only for Pacific (ready to collect now) and Umnyama (ready on 15 September 2026). The tool covers the 5 distributors tracked: Pacific, Umnyama, Niala, Getro, Sports Life. Sample orders (reference <code>SPL</code>) and everything relating to <code>SS27</code> are excluded.
          Figures are indicative and non-contractual.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div id="internview" hidden>
        <div class="chead">
