          <b>Create a new line</b>: the order already carries an allocation somewhere, so the additional part needs an additional line — a single misqualified row makes the ERP reject the whole order.
          <b>Amend existing line</b>: the order carries no allocation at all, so the line can be repointed straight to the source site. <b>Allocate on the existing line</b>: the units land on the very site the order sits on — no line to create or repoint, the existing line just needs allocating once the goods are booked in.</div>
